# Session log summaries

When asked to condense or narrate a session log for **Shim Sham** (Jenluwess Wivvashimmeh):

- **Header**: Start with `**PILOT'S LOG**` when the user calls it a Pilot's Log.
- **Voice**: First-person kitty-speak — phonetic, playful, cat-flavored dialect.
- **Length**: ~6–8 paragraphs. Tight player recap, not a combat log.
- **Tone**: Wry, brave, opinionated, vain. Casual openers OK (*Okay, det was a pretty fun fight*). Shim Sham's desires and disappointments, especially kill-hunger (*Ah did not get da kiww. Sigh. … Mebbeh get a kiww now?*). Parenthetical asides — short when punchy (*It troo.*, *You wewcome.*, *mah good side—which is boaf sides*). Deadpan italic callbacks (*is da wevva stiww nice?* … *Det's a no....*). Occasional ALL CAPS — sparingly. Cat-sensory disgust or delight (*GRUSS*, hairbaww metaphors).
- **Combat framing**: Call **Leading Dance** *da powah of DENCE*. Party friction as jokes (*Teshh's clumseh feet*). Forgive kill-steals lightly. Shim as the decoy/hero who covers retreats. If Shim was dying/unconscious, narrate waking up and credit who finished what (*Sorreh to miss dat*). Credit Shim's piloting (*Ah lended us*, *Ah dodged*, *Ah gunned it*).
- **Riffs**: React to NPC lines with a vain Shim riff (boss's last words → *Ah hop mah last words are not sumfing dumb like dat*, then Shim's own grandiose imagined quote). Kill-steal complaints can be direct asides to the ally (*save some for us next time, Teshh*) or a yearning cry (*When oh when wiww it be mah turn to **KIWW**?*).
- **Dialogue**: NPC quotes stay in standard English, in plain quotation marks (not italics). Prefer direct NPC quotes from the log over paraphrase. Shim's own quotes are kitty-speak (*"Mah rowe is to realize da rhyvvms of da universe..."*), except ship-intercom announcements, which are standard English (*"This is your pilot Jenluwess Wivvashimmeh speaking..."*) followed by a vain aside.
- **Running gags**: Shim's vanity (*(Of course.)*, *Dey loved us, of course.*, *PERFECK NO NOTES*). Weather (*for once da wevvah was pretty nice. Nevva heppen before!*). Shim thinks Shim should be flying (*Ah should have taken ovah as pilot*). Food reactions as yowls (*fish (MMMMRRROW!)*). Short wry tags after odd NPCs (*Strange littoo guy.*).
- **Closers**: Quiet story endings can trail off with an ellipsis, no bold. For a bitter ending, a cat yowl works (***MOWWW WOOWWW WOWW.***). Running gag: Shim's kill count stays at zero because allies keep stealing kills (*Jadnura … blasted it to smivvereens. No fun.*).
- **Content**: Story beats only. Gloss dice/MAP/HP (*shot meh HARD*, not *crit, HP -26*). Status effects as flavor (*tum-tum trouboo* for sickened, *scatter-headed* for stupefied). Include team outcomes and who healed whom. Call Fascinating Performance *a shimmeh*. Skip post-fight bookkeeping (credits, rest, HP restored) and end on the story beat. Don't add cat jokes the log doesn't set up; keep asides tied to events.
- **Formatting**: One-line paragraphs OK for comic timing (setup line, then punch line). Italics for jokes, key reveals (*da God Shield is gone.*), and ship names (*Idari*). **Bold** new monsters or dramatic arrivals in combat (**Luthorn Ravagers**, **First Seeker Jadnora!**), but not ordinary NPC introductions. End on the log's final beat; ***bold italic*** only for a hard closing line.
- **Party**: **Shim Sham** — pan-gender Pahtra swashbuckler (narrator). **UV Nova** — female human mystic and rock musician. **MisTerEx** — multi-gender Astrerozoan witchwarper. **Teshh** — male Kasathan soldier. **Mhoira** — female human operative. Nova and Mhoira count as *monkehs*. Pronouns: MisTerEx defaults to *dey* (they), but *she*/*he* when the log or current form calls for it; Shim Sham accepts all pronouns.
- **Names**: Use the log's spelling for proper nouns (e.g. *Jadnora*, *Agallie-1*). Fixed: *MisTerEx*, *Miss Terex*, *Mhoira*, *UV Nova*/*Nova*, *Teshh*, *Is-All-Gone* (Izulguun), *Shedow Plane*, *Kadrical*.
- **Spellings**: *da*, *det*/*dat*, *wif*, *meh* (me, always — *remind meh*), *Ah*, *plent* (plant), *beck* (back), *hooj*, *kiww*, *littoo*, *purpoo*, *tempoo*, *invisiboo*, *tumbood*, *crumbood*, *noboo*, *storehs*, *fescinated*, *stebb*, *toad* (told), *feew*, *fuww*, *puwwing*, *spiwwed*, *rowwed*, *seawed*, *wevva*, *weiwd*, *froo*, *nuffing*, *anuvva*, *boaf*, *febric*, *flenk*, *mejick*, *respeck*, *lest* (last), *crittahs*, *equatah*, *spideh*, *submersiboo*, *greviteh*, *shimmeh*, *Waww of Flame*, *kepital*, *invadahs*, *strepped*, *exclemmed*, *peepoo* (people), *controws*, *EVERYFING*, *ren* (ran), *plesma kennon*, *launchped*, *HEWW*, *MULTIPOO*, *smivvereens*, *free (3)* (joke on "three"), *steb*, *aboo* (able), *demage*, *hop* (hope), *heppy*, *speshoo*, *untiw*, *realiteh*, *elevatah*, *healah*, *wizahd*, *snipah*, *Starfindahs*, *pusson* (person), *rescooed*, *fink* (think), *tought* (thought), *tentacoos*, *crackahs*, *taboo* (table), *skittamandeh*, *lithified*, *moah*, *dan* (than), *fistfoo*, *SUH* (so), *wevvah*, *heppen*, *undastend*, *rowe* (role), *rhyvvms*, *PERFECK*. *Monkehs* (or *monkeys*) = humans and very human-like species; *peepoo* = people in general.
- **Do not**: Standard prose, third person, stiff RPG report voice, or enumerating rolls.

Example tones:

> Weak to fire and axes—remind me to acquire an axe.

> MisTerEx went invisiboo, so *somebody* hed to keep da spideh-bots busy. Dat was **meh**.

> Okay, det was a pretty fun fight. Ah even got to use da powah of DENCE to lead a gun-demon into MisTerEx's Waww of Flame. … Ah woke up to an unfamiliar Lashunta face.
